WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.988
If a CASE expression has no ELSE and no WHEN branch
matches

00:00:03.212 --> 00:00:08.700
PostgreSQL returns NULL That can be intentional when
NULL means unclassified but

00:00:08.712 --> 00:00:12.200
it can also create ambiguity if the analyst expected
a value such

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:17.575
as Other The example labels respiratory diagnoses
and leaves all other diagnoses

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:23.588
NULL Run it and inspect the unmatched rows Before
omitting ELSE decide

00:00:23.612 --> 00:00:27.888
what the missing result means The same idea applies
when the input

00:00:27.912 --> 00:00:31.888
can be NULL If a missing measure needs a separate
category such

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:35.238
as Needs review add an explicit NULL branch rather
than letting the

00:00:35.262 --> 00:00:36.912
value fall through accidentally
